        A key absent from values-xx resolves to values/, so a locale that has fallen behind still
        works in English. That is the same contract the desktop repository holds for its Qt
        catalogs, where an untranslated entry ships as type="unfinished" and Qt renders the source
        text, and the one tools/localization/audit_android_localizations.py reports as an advisory.
        Translation completeness is a backlog; a wrong translation is still a build failure, via
        ExtraTranslation here and the audit's placeholder-signature check.
    -->
